  "title": "So-called Temple of the Dioscuri",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/temple-2"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The temple belongs to the sacred area behind the so-called Theatre 3, and it is aligned with the altar beneath the latter. It was probably rebuilt a first time in the V century BC and then again in the II AD. Its name comes from a Chiot chalice dedicated to Castor and Pollux found during the excavations.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A temple on the acropolis of Cyrene, probably built around the seventh century BCE.",
